@page "/"

<PageTitle>Borm samples</PageTitle>

<h1>Borm samples</h1>

<p>
    One set of pages hosted unchanged by three Blazor Web Apps - <strong>Server</strong> (Interactive Server),
    <strong>Wasm</strong> (Interactive WebAssembly) and <strong>Auto</strong> (Interactive Auto), each prerendering
    first - and by a <strong>MAUI</strong> Blazor Hybrid app for Android, iOS, macOS and Windows. Every form behaves the
    same in each: Borm makes every decision in C# and has no JavaScript, so its rules run in the browser on WebAssembly,
    on the server over the circuit, and in the app's own process under MAUI. Only the static form is left out of the
    app, which has no server for it to post to.
</p>

<div class="card">
    <h2>Where this page is running</h2>
    <dl>
        <dt>Renderer</dt>
        <dd id="renderer">@RendererInfo.Name</dd>
        <dt>Interactive</dt>
        <dd id="interactive">@(RendererInfo.IsInteractive ? "yes" : AssignedRenderMode is null ? "no, rendered statically" : "no, prerendered")</dd>
    </dl>
    <p class="muted">
        Prerendered markup already holds every form as plain HTML: its rules, conditions and computed values start
        following the answers once the page is interactive.
    </p>
</div>

<h2>Samples</h2>
<ul>
    <li><NavLink href="generated">From a type</NavLink> - a whole form generated from a C# class and its DataAnnotations</li>
    <li><NavLink href="builder">Builder</NavLink> - the fluent builder: conditional fields, an async rule and a custom renderer</li>
    <li><NavLink href="wizard">Wizard</NavLink> - steps validated one at a time, a step only some answers need, and a review</li>
    <li><NavLink href="json-schema">JSON Schema</NavLink> - a form described as JSON, with a repeater and computed totals</li>
    @if (RendererInfo.Name is not "WebView")
    {
        <li><NavLink href="static-form">Static form</NavLink> - a form that posts to the server with no interactivity at all</li>
    }
</ul>
